Generate a standalone C reproducer that triggers this vulnerability:

File: bfd/cofflink.c
Line: 2284
Function: _bfd_coff_final_link
Bug type: heap-buffer-overflow
CWE: CWE-122
Explanation: Computes auxptr = flaginfo->outsyms + ((indx - syment_base + 1) * osymesz) and writes an aux entry to it via bfd_coff_swap_aux_out without checking that indx >= syment_base and that the computed position lies within the allocated outsyms buffer. A crafted input causing indx < syment_base or an otherwise out-of-range indx results in a write past the end of flaginfo->outsyms.

